ent.","short_summary":"Close Friday with a low-pressure look at Haverford's cross-disciplinary creative hub.","evidence_claim":"Haverford calls VCAM a 24/7 creative hub and lists flexible teaching and making spaces, including a presentation lounge, Create Spaces, and a Maker Arts Space.","source_url":"https://www.haverford.edu/vcam/about","source_title":"About | Visual Culture, Arts, and Media VCAM","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The College describes VCAM as a 24/7 hub; individual studios, equipment, and rooms may have separate access requirements.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"haverford-lutnick-library","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Allison & Howard Lutnick Library","title":"Map Your Study Base at Lutnick","subtitle":"Stop 5 · Saturday morning library orientation","notes":"Locate quiet reading rooms, group-study areas, printers, scanners, and reservable carrels before coursework begins to set your study routine.","short_summary":"Turn a Saturday walkthrough into a practical inventory of library services and study settings.","evidence_claim":"The Libraries' official page lists Lutnick Library's quiet reading rooms, collaborative rooms, reservable study carrels, computers, printers, scanners, and circulating collection.","source_url":"https://www.haverford.edu/libraries/places-hours","source_title":"Places & Hours | Haverford College Libraries","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Weekend and semester hours vary; confirm the live hours displayed on the Libraries page before visiting.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"haverford-nature-trail","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Haverford College Arboretum Nature Trail","title":"Walk the Nature Trail Loop","subtitle":"Stop 6 · Saturday late-morning campus circuit","notes":"Follow the 2.2-mile pedestrian trail around campus, keep bikes off the path, and use the loop to learn the college's outer edges.","short_summary":"Use the documented perimeter trail as both an outdoor break and a campus-orientation circuit.","evidence_claim":"The Arboretum welcomes the community to its 2.2-mile Nature Trail and states that the trail is pedestrian-only, with rules including no bicycle riding.","source_url":"https://www.haverford.edu/arboretum/faq","source_title":"FAQ | Arboretum","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The visitor guide lists the trail as open dawn to dusk; obey posted rules, leash pets, and stay off bicycles.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"haverford-duck-pond","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Duck Pond","title":"Pause at the Duck Pond","subtitle":"Stop 7 · Saturday midday nature stop","notes":"Stop beside the pond for a short wildlife observation, remain on established paths, and leave birds, plants, and other habitat undisturbed.","short_summary":"Break the longer outdoor circuit at a named Arboretum habitat documented in the visitor guide.","evidence_claim":"Haverford's Arboretum visitor guide identifies the Duck Pond as a 3.5-acre pond supporting native birds, mammals, fish, and reptiles.","source_url":"https://www.haverford.edu/sites/default/files/Office/Arboretum/Arboretum_VisitorsGuideTrifold23_FRO.pdf","source_title":"Haverford College Arboretum Visitor's Guide","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Visit during Arboretum dawn-to-dusk access and observe wildlife without feeding or approaching it.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"haverford-ryan-pinetum","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Ryan Pinetum","title":"Follow the Ryan Pinetum Markers","subtitle":"Stop 8 · Saturday afternoon tree walk","notes":"Enter the collection and follow the numbered posts through its highlighted areas; compare labels rather than collecting cones or plant material.","short_summary":"Add a self-guided route through Haverford's scientifically arranged living conifer collection.","evidence_claim":"The official Pinetum page describes an 18-acre scientific conifer collection and says numbered posts guide visitors through 15 areas of interest.","source_url":"https://www.haverford.edu/arboretum/arboretum-highlights/pinetum","source_title":"Pinetum | Arboretum","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Use the numbered outdoor route during Arboretum access hours and do not harvest plant material.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"haverford-cantor-fitzgerald-gallery","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Cantor Fitzgerald Gallery","title":"Take a Sunday Gallery Hour","subtitle":"Stop 9 · Sunday afternoon art visit","notes":"Enter through Whitehead Campus Center, spend one focused hour with the current exhibition, and note one work to discuss with a new classmate.","short_summary":"Give Sunday a defined cultural stop inside the campus center, with documented weekend access.","evidence_claim":"The gallery's official directions place it on Whitehead Campus Center's first floor and list Saturday and Sunday hours of noon–5:00 p.m.","source_url":"https://exhibits.haverford.edu/currently/hours-directions/","source_title":"Hours & Directions | Cantor Fitzgerald Gallery","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Current posted weekend hours are Saturday–Sunday, 12:00–5:00 p.m.; verify that an exhibition is installed before going.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"haverford-cope-field","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Cope Field","title":"Finish Beside Cope Field","subtitle":"Stop 10 · Sunday late-afternoon athletics landmark","notes":"End with a walk past the cricket pitch and Lester Pavilion; check the athletics schedule separately before planning to watch an actual match.","short_summary":"Close the sequence at a field tied to Haverford's unusually prominent varsity cricket program.","evidence_claim":"Haverford Athletics identifies Cope Field as the home of Haverford's cricket team and places the John A. Lester Cricket Pavilion and C. C. Morris Cricket Library there.","source_url":"https://haverfordathletics.com/sports/2025/5/16/information-facilites-cope-field.aspx","source_title":"Cope Field","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2025-05-16","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Field access may change for practices or competitions; consult current athletics schedules and posted facility rules.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
