 Nature Trail Loop","subtitle":"Stop 6 · Saturday late-morning campus circuit","notes":"Follow the 2.2-mile pedestrian trail around campus, keep bikes off the path, and use the loop to learn the college's outer edges.","short_summary":"Use the documented perimeter trail as both an outdoor break and a campus-orientation circuit.","evidence_claim":"The Arboretum welcomes the community to its 2.2-mile Nature Trail and states that the trail is pedestrian-only, with rules including no bicycle riding.","source_url":"https://www.haverford.edu/arboretum/faq","source_title":"FAQ | Arboretum","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The visitor guide lists the trail as open dawn to dusk; obey posted rules, leash pets, and stay off bicycles.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"haverford-duck-pond","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Duck Pond","title":"Pause at the Duck Pond","subtitle":"Stop 7 · Saturday midday nature stop","notes":"Stop beside the pond for a short wildlife observation, remain on established paths, and leave birds, plants, and other habitat undisturbed.","short_summary":"Break the longer outdoor circuit at a named Arboretum habitat documented in the visitor guide.","evidence_claim":"Haverford's Arboretum visitor guide identifies the Duck Pond as a 3.5-acre pond supporting native birds, mammals, fish, and reptiles.","source_url":"https://www.haverford.edu/sites/default/files/Office/Arboretum/Arboretum_VisitorsGuideTrifold23_FRO.pdf","source_title":"Haverford College Arboretum Visitor's Guide","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Visit during Arboretum dawn-to-dusk access and observe wildlife without feeding or approaching it.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{